values ('c1d2e3f4-5a6b-4c79-8e89-9f0a1b2c3d69', 'digital-imaging-photoshop', 'Digital Imaging (Photoshop)', 'Students learn Photoshop as a professional image-making environment for design, photography, illustration, and visual communication, and build technical literacy in pixels, resolution, compression, color modes, and output-ready files. The course covers non-destructive layers, precise selections and masks, tonal and color correction, ethical retouching, compositing, type and layout integration, experimental effects, RAW and cross-app production, concept-driven image strategy, rights and inclusive practice, and delivery for print, web, social, and portfolio. Critique and a finished image series synthesize those skills.');

