  'Students learn Photoshop as a professional image-making environment for design, photography, illustration, and visual communication, and build technical literacy in pixels, resolution, compression, color modes, and output-ready files. The course covers non-destructive layers, precise selections and masks, tonal and color correction, ethical retouching, compositing, type and layout integration, experimental effects, RAW and cross-app production, concept-driven image strategy, rights and inclusive practice, and delivery for print, web, social, and portfolio. Critique and a finished image series synthesize those skills.',
  $dimgjson${"slug": "digital-imaging-photoshop", "title": "Digital Imaging (Photoshop)", "description": "Students learn Photoshop as a professional image-making environment for design, photography, illustration, and visual communication, and build technical literacy in pixels, resolution, compression, color modes, and output-ready files. The course covers non-destructive layers, precise selections and masks, tonal and color correction, ethical retouching, compositing, type and layout integration, experimental effects, RAW and cross-app production, concept-driven image strategy, rights and inclusive practice, and delivery for print, web, social, and portfolio. Critique and a finished image series synthesize those skills.", "topics": [{"id": "52398aa2-7725-40dc-91b3-876805c70da8", "type": "topic", "title": "Digital Imaging Foundations and Photoshop Workspace", "description": "Understand Photoshop as a professional image-making environment for design, photography, illustration, and visual communication.", "children": [{"id": "918d27fc-c890-45de-b959-f3b5cf6d07cd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Photoshop as a design tool", "children": [{"id": "33ec8d5b-de26-4227-9b2b-9f4d96c7e6ce", "type": "concept", "title": "Raster image editing in graphic design, photography, illustration, advertising, publishing, and social media"}, {"id": "4f7ab55d-ba1e-45d0-90eb-ca8b37b4d7dd", "type": "concept", "title": "Relationship among Photoshop, Illustrator, InDesign, Lightroom, Bridge, and web platforms"}, {"id": "c9e630c5-aaa5-4045-8847-1762bf1f2842", "type": "concept", "title": "When Photoshop is the right tool and when a vector, layout, motion, or web tool is better"}], "description": "This subtopic frames Photoshop as a visual communication environment, not only a software checklist."}, {"id": "01c3a322-e87a-4a1f-9582-160e2c4d22f3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Workspace fluency", "children": [{"id": "0e120467-8815-44fb-a13d-5f14c2a13e09", "type": "concept", "title": "Tools panel, options bar, contextual task bar, layers panel, properties panel, adjustments, channels, paths, and history"}, {"id": "fb90622c-3f40-49ee-8ed4-06d6d08ce9e4", "type": "concept", "title": "Workspace customization, keyboard shortcuts, tool presets, guides, rulers, grids, and snapping"}, {"id": "56449045-fa0b-4429-bda2-719b4b71b643", "type": "concept", "title": "Zoom, pan, rotate view, screen modes, multiple documents, and comparison views"}], "description": "Students learn where tools, panels, preferences, and shortcuts live so attention can shift from menus to visual decisions."}, {"id": "850d35ca-5456-4d21-9f80-b2e658b9dbe9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Professional file habits", "children": [{"id": "ea278dae-6405-4aa4-acdf-4d8e506baa73", "type": "concept", "title": "Project folders, original assets, working files, exports, linked files, and final deliverables"}, {"id": "1a51ce08-c1bd-4355-a262-b9e11192ddfb", "type": "concept", "title": "Layer naming, groups, color labels, notes, version numbers, and saved milestones"}, {"id": "69bdbae3-1954-487e-baea-ee5efc2b96ce", "type": "concept", "title": "Common mistakes: editing originals, flattening too early, losing links, and exporting the wrong size"}], "description": "Strong Photoshop practice begins with organized files, named layers, versioning, and backups."}]}, {"id": "b580a268-6880-4428-853c-e9b80dacd4ca", "type": "topic", "title": "Raster Image Fundamentals, Resolution, Color Modes, and File Formats", "description": "Build technical literacy around pixels, resolution, compression, bit depth, color modes, and output-ready files.", "children": [{"id": "016a99a9-b258-45bf-948c-8ab036dd95f1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Pixels and resolution", "children": [{"id": "b8e708ec-90ee-4e2b-90ca-7e907376c8d4", "type": "concept", "title": "Pixels, image dimensions, ppi, dpi, resampling, interpolation, aspect ratio, and crop ratios"}, {"id": "388bba6b-313f-4fea-b928-692df973dcda", "type": "concept", "title": "Screen resolution versus print resolution and why 72 ppi myths persist"}, {"id": "70e997cd-6ca6-49d9-9fca-4f24cb239ef5", "type": "concept", "title": "Sharpening, noise, softness, and the limits of upscaling"}], "description": "Resolution determines how an image holds detail across screens, print, cropping, and enlargement."}, {"id": "c2e3e88b-238e-46ee-a3e6-eaff77d57bb2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Color modes and bit depth", "children": [{"id": "6f00c355-7f59-4fc2-8965-593cca8f9310", "type": "concept", "title": "RGB, CMYK, grayscale, Lab, indexed color, duotone, spot color, and Pantone workflows"}, {"id": "2a95e892-d8d0-4fc8-b484-1735f7d3a115", "type": "concept", "title": "8-bit, 16-bit, 32-bit, dynamic range, banding, and tonal precision"}, {"id": "8a189941-ac19-48ac-9b4b-aeb4245445e3", "type": "concept", "title": "Color gamut, profiles, soft proofing, and conversion risks"}], "description": "Color modes affect what colors are available, how edits behave, and where a file can be used."}, {"id": "9829e3d5-2101-4fdd-a339-928910e1f681", "type": "subtopic", "title": "File formats and compression", "children": [{"id": "d8736c39-f36e-4786-a356-805d11896215", "type": "concept", "title": "PSD, PSB, TIFF, JPEG, PNG, GIF, PDF, HEIC, WebP, RAW, DNG, and SVG-adjacent workflows"}, {"id": "2e3f023a-a7da-4e15-b9a6-9f9b4fba1e91", "type": "concept", "title": "Lossless versus lossy compression, transparency, layers, metadata, and archive value"}, {"id": "b9bd6e15-c07b-4d51-b1e3-4fc4fef163ab", "type": "concept", "title": "Working file, production file, delivery file, and thumbnail file distinctions"}], "description": "Students learn to choose file formats by purpose instead of habit."}]}, {"id": "da92dce6-06b9-49a8-8d6e-6359e10353be", "type": "topic", "title": "Non-Destructive Workflow, Layers, Smart Objects, and Organization", "description": "Develop disciplined file structures that keep images editable, reversible, and production-ready.", "children": [{"id": "294d3ebc-e9ad-43b0-851f-5ca8ddbcda0a"