tle": "Layer comps, alternate looks, revision files, and documenting edit decisions"}], "description": "Non-destructive adjustment helps students test visual directions and revise based on critique."}]}, {"id": "cd021746-bf32-4ea3-9345-3d92f3994a27", "type": "topic", "title": "Selections, Masks, Channels, and Edge Refinement", "description": "Learn how precise isolation and masking make sophisticated correction, retouching, and compositing possible.", "children": [{"id": "768efe22-ad09-4ea6-8412-75c4d586b48d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Selection tools and judgment", "children": [{"id": "1cf52302-6186-4d53-b340-c9b825826e1b", "type": "concept", "title": "Marquee, lasso, object selection, quick selection, magic wand, pen paths, color range, focus area, and select subject"}, {"id": "da7f5e55-976c-43cf-92b2-387c414737bc", "type": "concept", "title": "Hard edges, soft edges, hair, transparent objects, shadows, reflections, and motion blur"}, {"id": "702ad00f-6112-46e4-8a46-593bb74edba0", "type": "concept", "title": "Adding, subtracting, intersecting, feathering, smoothing, expanding, and contracting selections"}], "description": "Selections are the foundation for isolating image areas, but students must choose the tool that fits the edge."}, {"id": "bb1334d9-4444-4ca3-a9a8-b8f9ae2eed1e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Layer masks and vector masks", "children": [{"id": "be802438-a997-4eaa-8896-7656d9e62da2", "type": "concept", "title": "White, black, and gray mask logic; brushwork on masks; mask density and feather"}, {"id": "60b78602-1418-412e-bb9d-616001f2f9cc", "type": "concept", "title": "Vector masks, paths, shape edges, and combining raster and vector masks"}, {"id": "b34d9f5b-ed81-48da-8452-3212d9a4438f", "type": "concept", "title": "Clipping masks, nested masks, adjustment masks, and mask troubleshooting"}], "description": "Masks teach students to hide and reveal information without deleting it."}, {"id": "9b1abe75-d69d-4bc5-acd9-323126abd1a5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Channels and advanced edge work", "children": [{"id": "c618332b-7572-418e-84e9-7c9171394bf5", "type": "concept", "title": "Alpha channels, luminosity masks, channel calculations, contrast-based masks, and blend-if controls"}, {"id": "dc352659-c211-41c6-b37f-bd938cbf9b26", "type": "concept", "title": "Select and Mask workspace, refine edge brush, decontaminate colors, and hair/fur/fabric edges"}, {"id": "4edfef4e-29f3-4f62-898b-5f682bdb7089", "type": "concept", "title": "Checking masks against black, white, color, and transparent backgrounds"}], "description": "Channels give students a deeper route into complex selections and image structure."}]}, {"id": "387ba246-c92d-4b9b-9e3e-e5e5b372b8db", "type": "topic", "title": "Tonal Correction, Color Correction, and Color Management", "description": "Control contrast, exposure, color balance, and device-dependent color so images reproduce with intention.", "children": [{"id": "f10e385f-b69d-4608-ad4b-161ce90271cd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Tonal structure", "children": [{"id": "a860ecb8-1c30-446a-b096-01267de0ef82", "type": "concept", "title": "Histogram reading, levels, curves, exposure, contrast, black point, white point, midtones, highlight recovery, and shadow detail"}, {"id": "91c6bcd3-d279-4a7a-84c6-e68b7cbd9743", "type": "concept", "title": "Local versus global correction, dodge and burn, luminosity control, and tonal separation"}, {"id": "3e6b2dc5-eaf9-489f-ae0d-27233cdcd0bf", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding crushed shadows, clipped highlights, muddy midtones, and overprocessed contrast"}], "description": "Tone correction establishes whether an image has usable detail, hierarchy, and visual depth."}, {"id": "b48a25c6-1ea8-4a95-b846-315971ae6eae", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Color correction", "children": [{"id": "0aef54c1-f452-4ac0-97ad-11fc28d4435d", "type": "concept", "title": "White balance, neutral correction, color casts, skin tone, product color, memory color, and palette matching"}, {"id": "21e2a0b3-1b65-4ab2-876b-7c0859ca3bbd", "type": "concept", "title": "Hue/saturation, vibrance, selective color, color balance, gradient maps, and camera profiles"}, {"id": "1ec7de60-2059-4818-875e-543c74b7b35b", "type": "concept", "title": "Color grading versus correction and matching multiple images in a series"}], "description": "Color correction teaches students to make images accurate, expressive, or system-consistent."}, {"id": "b47db294-5dd2-4c75-96b8-5692500f0cd3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Color management", "children": [{"id": "7178497e-721b-4c58-9ee9-d6de79d9da27", "type": "concept", "title": "ICC profiles, working spaces, sRGB, Adobe RGB, Display P3, CMYK profiles, soft proofing, and rendering intents"}, {"id": "4914ab8f-e7bc-400b-86fa-c90ea7489e2b", "type": "concept", "title": "Monitor calibration, proof setup, gamut warning, rich black, total ink limit, and profile conversion"}, {"id": "cddc3c15-40a2-4003-924c-1488fd02d5df", "type": "concept", "title": "Communicating color requirements with printers, clients, developers, and collaborators"}], "description": "Color management connects screen decisions to print, web, and production reality."}]}, {"id": "eb35c721-ff19-4e88-a4df-6e1f6f1c576a", "type": "topic", "title": "Retouching, Restoration, and Image Cleanup", "description": "Use ethical, controlled retouching methods to repair, clarify, and enhance images without destroying credibility.", "children": [{"id": "5d3c1a74-ffaf-4960-a009-5f8a98fb10c4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Core retouching tools", "children": [{"id": "dfc935b3-c109-488b-8731-c9821a5b03da", "type": "concept", "title": "Clone stamp, healing brush, spot healing, patch tool, content-aware fill, remove tool, and generative-style removal awareness"}, {"id": "ae7bbc00-cd31-4bda-8909-956c2bfba30f", "type": "concept", "title": "Sampling, alignment, texture preservation, frequency awareness, and working on blank retouching layers"}, {"id": "8097e3db-3ae8-491d-a4e7-c4dc82802182", "type": "concept", "title": "Dust, scratches, blemishes, distractions, seams, sensor spots, and background cleanup"}], "description": "Students learn cleanup tools as controlled interventions rather than automatic fixes."}, {"id": "8bc30475-7e9f-4c45-b537-4f313e00aef3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Portrait and product retouching", "children": [{"id": "aacc08cf-5c79-47f2-b433-ce2bc2f10bff", "type": "concept", "title": "Skin texture, flyaways, wardrobe distractions, reflections, product surfaces, labels, symmetry, and edges"}, {"id": "bcc75274-6239-40b2-98b9-e0b611c9ccce", "type": "concept", "title": "Frequency separation basics, dodge and burn, liquify restraint, color cleanup, and realistic shadow work"}, {"id": "e7268af0-823d-46e6-b54d-e31948f01d7e", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethical boundaries for beauty, documentary, editorial, product, and archival contexts"}], "description": "Retouching should support communication goals while respecting texture, identity, and credibility."}, {"id": "d01777c6-1768-457a-b8bb-6407bc0d4d3a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Restoration and repair", "children": [{"id": "9b477d3a-680d-43e3-8217-56fee94826b1", "type": "concept", "title": "Scanning, dust and scratch removal, tear repair, tonal restoration, color fading, stains, missing areas, and grain management"}, {"id": "7372733e-0f24-45da-a0b0-1328041cc78e", "type": "concept", "title": "Working from duplicate layers, preserving source files, and comparing before/after states"}, {"id": "9112d7ed-1f80-424b-ace7-3660af31c0a2", "type": "concept", "title": "Metadata, provenance, uncertainty, and when not to over-restore"}], "description": "Restoration teaches students to reconstruct damaged images while documenting assumptions."}]}, {"id": "31933ded-7df8-4d5b-81b2-c728897352a4", "type": "topic", "title": "Compositing, Photomontage, and Constructed Images", "description": "Combine images into persuasive, believable, or intentionally expressive composites with coherent light, scale, and perspective.", "children": [{"id": "b2e2b654-1524-4d11-8e8f-c1cc622dce4e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Composite construction", "children": [{"id": "d4f6e7a1-7811-4a40-8d71-185f56b8234e", "type": "concept", "title": "Cutouts, masks, perspective, scale, horizon, depth cues, vanishing points, and spatial logic"}, {"id": "ea702d0e-2918-49dc-8756-8accc15875c6", "type": "concept", "title": "Light direction, shadow shape, contact shadows, reflected light, color temperature, grain, sharpness, and atmospheric perspective"}, {"id": "1f0c010f-210a-4f66-8501-f0699dbfdea0", "type": "concept", "title": "Believable realism, surreal collage, editorial montage, and conceptual image construction"}], "description": "Compositing asks students to make many pieces behave as one visual world or one purposeful collage."}, {"id": "3210024e-dcaf-4fd0-a5ee-9f41792c37d4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Blend modes and transparency", "children": [{"id": "0f219898-d6c9-4d9a-9b39-09531316d847", "type": "concept", "title": "Multiply, screen, overlay, soft light, hard light, color, luminosity, difference, and normal blend behavior"}, {"id": "fc254c4b-915e-4dbb-8aa1-081965db7a24", "type": "concept", "title": "Texture overlays, double exposure, tonal blending, color blending, and blend-if sliders"}, {"id": "c40fabaf-cf06-4990-9ec7-42e0883b969b", "type": "concept", "title": "Opacity, fill, clipping, masks, and stacking order interactions"}], "description": "Blend modes are image mathematics that can become powerful visual language when used deliberately."}, {"id": "86756507-95a1-40f6-8967-42202b2a6067", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Photomontage and meaning", "children": [{"id": "28723522-d217-4622-b719-e7bb760956da", "type": "concept", "title": "Juxtaposition, metaphor, sequence, scale shift, archival fragments, found imagery, and visual rhetoric"}, {"id": "8528fbbf-04b2-4d00-9cbf-c34b694e5318", "type": "concept", "title": "Dada, surrealism, political montage, advertising, album art, posters, and contemporary digital collage"}, {"id": "41f76307-1df6-4ecb-869f-84653e32506e", "type": "concept", "title": "Credit, permissions, appropriation, transformation, and audience interpretation"}], "description": "Constructed images carry arguments, narratives, and cultural references."}]}, {"id": "450a0ede-187e-4210-a891-4f561a9605f5", "type": "topic", "title": "Type, Graphics, Layout, and Design Integration", "description": "Integrate raster images with typography, vector graphics, hierarchy, grids, and brand or editorial systems.", "children": [{"id": "2115ce65-c69e-4eee-a369-3cbed0d687ec", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Type in Photoshop", "children": [{"id": "beaee581-db39-485f-ae94-1ea33290c5bf", "type": "concept", "title": "Type layers, character and paragraph panels, alignment, tracking, leading, hierarchy, legibility, and rasterization risks"}, {"id": "7e9bdb61-8a70-49d5-b0d0-ae804e5ae340", "type": "concept", "title": "Type masks, clipping images into type, text effects, and title treatments"}, {"id": "473091cb-7874-485d-8e59-c246f06bc82a", "type": "concept", "title": "Handing off type-heavy work to Illustrator, InDesign, Figma, or layout tools when needed"}], "description": "Students learn when Photoshop type is appropriate and how to keep it readable, editable, and production-safe."}, {"id": "5d2b4f75-ee64-47df-a121-d93a67f7e831", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Graphic elements and hierarchy", "children": [{"id": "90868826-7d6f-413c-9ca8-dea653c245be", "type": "concept", "title": "Shapes, strokes, gradients, patterns, icons, grids, guides, margins, visual hierarchy, scale, and alignment"}, {"id": "20e84a03-6f44-48a1-86b9-a77b009169a3", "type": "concept", "title": "Poster, social tile, editorial opener, album cover, event graphic, and campaign mockup contexts"}, {"id": "484680d7-b1ab-4939-ade6-f45085340f77", "type": "concept", "title": "Balancing image, type, logo, caption, call to action, and negative space"}], "description": "Image edits become design when they are organized into a communicative hierarchy."}, {"id": "24c4f6e4-4fdf-449e-b595-02a56efe5c9c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Design system integration", "children": [{"id": "f2841bea-36f8-4273-8d05-6fc1de222509", "type": "concept", "title": "Brand colors, type systems, asset libraries, style guides, templates, smart mockups, and artboards"}, {"id": "c8493256-7ca2-4747-9c00-50859475f245", "type": "concept", "title": "Consistency across print, web, social, presentation, and portfolio outputs"}, {"id": "315d20e5-5c9d-4f30-887a-6669eec7bddd", "type": "concept", "title": "Exporting layered assets for collaborators while preserving editability"}], "description": "Photoshop work often lives inside larger identity systems and multi-format campaigns."}]}, {"id": "2f0b71df-38c1-460b-bb9a-56eeb812c0b5", "type": "topic", "title": "Filters, Effects, Texture, and Experimental Image-Making", "description": "Use effects and image transformations as deliberate visual language rather than decoration.", "children": [{"id": "71f3296d-dcc1-45d5-a223-df6e9b360e8d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Filters as process", "children": [{"id": "e168784c-f8f6-4bdd-a9f1-295ed89267f1", "type": "concept", "title": "Blur, sharpen, noise, distort, liquify, displacement, render, neural-style tools, and Camera Raw filter"}, {"id": "a862cccc-4672-40ae-9bc9-cd71ef203360", "type": "concept", "title": "Smart Filters, filter masks, stacking filters, and maintaining reversibility"}, {"id": "16e2b47e-1329-4677-a9cd-6fff6bef2711", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding default-looking effects, cliches, and accidental overprocessing"}], "description": "Filters become useful when students understand what they do and why an effect supports the image."}, {"id": "b2e786a1-b531-4556-ade6-767b24162421", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Texture and surface", "children": [{"id": "6ae06e44-0dba-4f3a-9a75-7f18b6324288", "type": "concept", "title": "Grain, paper, halftone, scan artifacts, paint texture, photocopy effects, scratches, and overlays"}, {"id": "24929e7f-36f7-492e-9ae4-da4b77ebeca7", "type": "concept", "title": "Displacement maps, blending texture into light and shadow, and matching texture across elements"}, {"id": "9dae53f1-d84f-4235-b40b-c3c7ea340b63", "type": "concept", "title": "Using texture for mood, authenticity, history, or critique"}], "description": "Texture gives digital images material presence and can connect work to print, photography, drawing, and collage."}, {"id": "458bff6c-08cc-4dd3-a7ce-a61c284711d3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Experimental workflows", "children": [{"id": "c50e66e6-1f28-4f15-bdd8-5bf7e6ffb19c", "type": "concept", "title": "Glitch, scanography, data bending awareness, generative patterns, procedural textures, and collage systems"}, {"id": "fba8db19-0c52-4b65-add2-440d9ebdd205", "type": "concept", "title": "Iteration, chance operations, constraints, batch processing, and image series development"}, {"id": "e1c0155d-e83b-4bb7-ab5a-4c1048ca7b26", "type": "concept", "title": "Documenting process so experiments become design knowledge"}], "description": "Experimental imaging expands Photoshop beyond correction into studio practice."}]}, {"id": "1a2aebdd-6b22-4738-9e94-e1443cb4a1f5", "type": "topic", "title": "Photography Workflow, RAW Processing, and Cross-App Production", "description": "Connect Photoshop to camera files, Lightroom, Bridge, Illustrator, InDesign, and portfolio workflows.", "children": [{"id": "a01faf42-3497-4361-bb93-cb3a0d88c169", "type": "subtopic", "title": "RAW and camera workflow", "children": [{"id": "40dfb1a5-cd3c-4863-bef3-cf916459c262", "type": "concept", "title": "RAW files, DNG, Camera Raw, white balance, exposure, lens corrections, noise reduction, and sharpening"}, {"id": "d8be4f5f-5513-4ad4-8ff0-74b885f9586c", "type": "concept", "title": "Lightroom and Bridge workflows, selects, ratings, keywords, collections, and contact sheets"}, {"id": "a3307b56-7261-4685-9e32-b030f721ef02", "type": "concept", "title": "From capture to edit: naming, importing, backing up, and preserving originals"}], "description": "Students learn how source image quality affects every downstream Photoshop decision."}, {"id": "2ae1c67e-43c1-424c-a376-7c3d9833cacb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cross-app workflows", "children": [{"id": "4fb3ac03-428b-497e-be38-f685a6304e43", "type": "concept", "title": "Photoshop with Lightroom, Bridge, Illustrator, InDesign, Acrobat, Figma, After Effects, and web CMS tools"}, {"id": "b0cf3ed9-0e3d-4d6f-b244-30f4a05f95dd", "type": "concept", "title": "Linked assets, placed files, copy-paste risks, embedded color profiles, and export handoff"}, {"id": "df46bfd5-1284-4379-9f5f-3bedb49d09c2", "type": "concept", "title": "Packaging, shared folders, cloud documents, version conflicts, and collaborative review"}], "description": "Professional image work often moves among several tools and collaborators."}, {"id": "0bf81f12-1835-440b-8acf-09bc0301a4bd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Image series consistency", "children": [{"id": "731747fc-91c7-40a2-b664-068c06e00bbe", "type": "concept", "title": "Batch edits, actions, presets, synchronized Camera Raw settings, contact sheets, and visual consistency"}, {"id": "efe6e085-2218-4fda-945f-0289b3187753", "type": "concept", "title": "Matching crop, tone, color, grain, shadows, product angles, backgrounds, and naming conventions"}, {"id": "5c1c0866-ec8e-40bd-b549-f8d6ed5881c1", "type": "concept", "title": "Series logic for portfolios, campaigns, social posts, editorial packages, and exhibitions"}], "description": "Designers often need sets of images to feel related, not just individual hero images."}]}, {"id": "d2dd215f-1cf0-4618-b51b-459cbee04a44", "type": "topic", "title": "Visual Research, Concept Development, and Image Strategy", "description": "Move beyond software exercises into concept-driven image systems that solve communication problems.", "children": [{"id": "b008f921-375c-4897-9f82-f4fd84a38c07", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Research and references", "children": [{"id": "064e7e58-2b40-4903-a039-02d3b84c4efa", "type": "concept", "title": "Mood boards, precedent studies, image banks, artist references, design history, photography references, and campaign analysis"}, {"id": "7a7c4893-7413-4feb-86b4-2b9f82dfed56", "type": "concept", "title": "Research ethics, source tracking, reference transformation, and avoiding plagiarism"}, {"id": "a0fb9019-e4e5-4fb1-954e-0693457dabfe", "type": "concept", "title": "Reading an image for audience, tone, genre, medium, and cultural context"}], "description": "Visual research helps students make informed choices rather than copying surface style."}, {"id": "aed659b7-7d2e-458d-8a54-77451979c0bf", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Concept development", "children": [{"id": "2ccf98a4-6640-4d17-9c5e-c0a7e29205a4", "type": "concept", "title": "Brief analysis, audience, message, constraints, deliverables, keywords, sketches, thumbnails, and concept boards"}, {"id": "d09bd5ec-324b-4c44-b499-56353aaff3e0", "type": "concept", "title": "Choosing image strategy: documentary, surreal, clean product, editorial, expressive, archival, or typographic"}, {"id": "5c2fa1a7-3307-4f5b-af20-bbab93eaf96c", "type": "concept", "title": "Testing multiple directions and selecting based on criteria rather than taste alone"}], "description": "Photoshop projects should start with a communication problem or artistic question."}, {"id": "095ef42f-1fcc-49d5-b203-e9b7ad8defc1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Image systems", "children": [{"id": "6d400773-0a48-4e1c-95a2-8baabff7215a", "type": "concept", "title": "Series, sequence, variation, campaign family, visual rules, templates, and modular assets"}, {"id": "b2eea37c-3152-415a-b621-03397e83bd2d", "type": "concept", "title": "Consistency and surprise, rhythm and contrast, hierarchy and repetition"}, {"id": "e078d5c0-70bc-4aeb-9598-b7468f96ab14", "type": "concept", "title": "Connecting image strategy to typography, color, brand, platform, and context"}], "description": "World-class design programs ask students to build systems, not only one-off images."}]}, {"id": "0164bab3-ed7f-43eb-99bc-101c43f6e173", "type": "topic", "title": "Ethics, Copyright, Inclusive Imagery, and AI-Aware Practice", "description": "Build responsible habits around manipulation, authorship, consent, representation, accessibility, and emerging tools.", "children": [{"id": "ca1cb874-62d1-4768-916d-4af6191fc2b5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Manipulation ethics", "children": [{"id": "618e7faf-d71d-4cf5-92e6-e763e756d909", "type": "concept", "title": "Editorial versus advertising standards, documentary truth claims, disclosure, body image, product accuracy, and archival integrity"}, {"id": "77fa3832-eeed-4d8a-b1c5-497d8f65a272", "type": "concept", "title": "Before/after transparency, retouching boundaries, and context-dependent expectations"}, {"id": "32393d4a-8bdf-4d7a-b9d2-bc6392dece13", "type": "concept", "title": "Consequences of misleading edits for trust, identity, culture, and public information"}], "description": "Image editing changes how viewers understand reality, people, products, events, and evidence."}, {"id": "0eb8d800-c2eb-4909-8e54-9d4c01860854", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Rights and authorship", "children": [{"id": "f379a65e-67d6-469a-949e-0f4e0690c786", "type": "concept", "title": "Copyright, fair use, licenses, Creative Commons, public domain, model releases, property releases, trademarks, and attribution"}, {"id": "9db42937-1413-4f58-ae17-c1c666be3797", "type": "concept", "title": "Stock imagery, archives, museum collections, dataset provenance, and client-provided assets"}, {"id": "5f13d3be-671a-4cd7-9e2f-1a26ca442cc9", "type": "concept", "title": "Maintaining source logs and documenting permissions"}], "description": "Students need practical copyright literacy before using found images, fonts, textures, and generated assets."}, {"id": "073034e1-6290-4c62-9322-d0e816c571f6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inclusive and AI-aware practice", "children": [{"id": "7c7fe373-b581-4ce2-bf98-5a6c95ca9433", "type": "concept", "title": "Inclusive imagery, stereotypes, skin-tone handling, cultural context, disability representation, and accessibility of visual communication"}, {"id": "e9f65d07-2348-44e2-a8c6-8ff725f7f476", "type": "concept", "title": "Alt text, captions, contrast, readable type, and platform accessibility requirements"}, {"id": "04370056-4c42-4d3d-8f06-58860f31961b", "type": "concept", "title": "Generative fill, AI-assisted retouching, synthetic imagery, bias, disclosure, provenance, and human judgment"}], "description": "Responsible digital imaging includes accessibility, representation, and careful use of emerging tools."}]}, {"id": "b7b856f2-b093-49a0-a812-a1dcb265033e", "type": "topic", "title": "Output for Print, Web, Social, and Portfolio Delivery", "description": "Prepare images for real production contexts with correct formats, profiles, dimensions, metadata, and quality control.", "children": [{"id": "72f3b0a9-7f14-469e-98a1-b84a979c46ab", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Print output", "children": [{"id": "80ff3520-dd59-4111-aa19-dd475f76d4f5", "type": "concept", "title": "CMYK conversion, spot colors, bleed, trim, crop marks, rich black, overprint awareness, resolution, sharpening, and PDF export"}, {"id": "5de3dbbb-ac19-4c68-af06-4f6dd241d1b1", "type": "concept", "title": "Printer specifications, proofing, paper, ink behavior, and communicating with production partners"}, {"id": "3f07c2ce-5720-4efe-9ed3-245939cc53ea", "type": "concept", "title": "Poster, postcard, book cover, package mockup, and exhibition print contexts"}], "description": "Print production requires different thinking from screen-only images."}, {"id": "a92f4fb6-f57f-4ed1-a579-b862e2e18372", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Screen and web output", "children": [{"id": "a47de917-26a4-4d4e-a5ae-201725ae8d63", "type": "concept", "title": "sRGB, Display P3 awareness, JPEG, PNG, WebP, GIF, dimensions, compression, retina assets, thumbnails, and metadata"}, {"id": "1e57f115-8c9c-4445-96e1-83e6943bddcf", "type": "concept", "title": "Social platform sizes, responsive images, accessibility, file-size limits, and compression artifacts"}, {"id": "7605de52-3581-4621-99dd-801307cbb9d4", "type": "concept", "title": "Testing exports on multiple screens and in real upload contexts"}], "description": "Digital delivery requires balancing quality, speed, compatibility, and platform constraints."}, {"id": "8d992c7e-b509-4ede-a681-ce1fb2f696d2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Quality control and archiving", "children": [{"id": "4053f968-4745-4be1-a453-37e2d7a31349", "type": "concept", "title": "Export checklists, spelling, visible artifacts, color shifts, missing fonts, wrong dimensions, and flattened copies"}, {"id": "d75fbe87-cc08-4494-a8c4-6afc4b1a3a1e", "type": "concept", "title": "Working files, master files, delivery files, previews, contact sheets, and archive folders"}, {"id": "1b361c82-f355-4d1c-9b14-2af9fffe9dfe", "type": "concept", "title": "Metadata, version history, licensing notes, and portfolio documentation"}], "description": "Final delivery should be checked, named, and archived so work can be reused later."}]}, {"id": "aad24ce4-8ec4-4ecb-9b05-df0945de951c", "type": "topic", "title": "Critique, Iteration, Documentation, and Portfolio Presentation", "description": "Use critique and process documentation to refine work and present digital imaging decisions professionally.", "children": [{"id": "1e82bfc2-1241-400d-9e8f-1ddbf6e2e52b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Critique methods", "children": [{"id": "5a6db69a-89fd-4273-885f-d7eb1d8c38cf", "type": "concept", "title": "Descriptive, analytical, interpretive, and evaluative feedback"}, {"id": "0beb2c28-d0df-44a1-9ce9-bf000122e9be", "type": "concept", "title": "Discussing composition, color, tone, mask quality, image credibility, hierarchy, and concept"}, {"id": "93c12072-4fc2-40d7-894b-97d861e20227", "type": "concept", "title": "Giving actionable feedback and receiving critique without losing project ownership"}], "description": "Critique teaches students to connect visual decisions to intention, audience, craft, and ethics."}, {"id": "c0b5d3ad-ce99-4871-8bc2-17d62f3c0ac7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Revision and process documentation", "children": [{"id": "b917195f-0be9-435f-85a0-3f027b63edc2", "type": "concept", "title": "Before/after states, process screenshots, version notes, layer organization, source logs, and reflection memos"}, {"id": "2350f239-bcf9-4624-8544-1cbe49945844", "type": "concept", "title": "Revision priorities: concept, hierarchy, color, mask quality, retouching, typography, output, and ethics"}, {"id": "009651f1-6c74-4a29-b759-9cc6659d0995", "type": "concept", "title": "Using critique to decide what to simplify, intensify, rebuild, or abandon"}], "description": "Iteration is how software skill becomes design judgment."}, {"id": "7c275a77-c3a6-46ed-9f79-2f9bda5306ec", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Portfolio presentation", "children": [{"id": "0b199085-3873-44e6-a9be-92f207503c33", "type": "concept", "title": "Project title, brief, role, tools, process, final images, mockups, and outcome"}, {"id": "d4696654-09f6-4264-9a3c-f24995cac866", "type": "concept", "title": "Image sequencing, captions, thumbnails, case-study layout, and credit lines"}, {"id": "d9230b69-2683-4749-a3b7-aa190e07f509", "type": "concept", "title": "Preparing work for Behance, personal sites, PDF portfolios, interviews, and class reviews"}], "description": "A strong portfolio shows both finished images and the thinking behind them."}]}, {"id": "2fe9b8b0-45d1-4867-956e-145da60ba585", "type": "topic", "title": "Final Digital Imaging Project or Image Series Capstone", "description": "Synthesize technical, conceptual, ethical, and production skills in a finished image series or campaign-ready project.", "children": [{"id": "4a4b3c1d-a87f-48c3-b90d-bedb4bdf375c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Project proposal", "children": [{"id": "2fd10366-683c-4ea2-b84a-189f4d9b603d", "type": "concept", "title": "Creative brief, concept statement, audience, mood board, source plan, rights plan, technical goals, and schedule"}, {"id": "1f396d1f-6b9e-4540-a9b7-d455e43bdb07", "type": "concept", "title": "Image series, poster campaign, editorial feature, brand system, album cover, social campaign, or exhibition set"}, {"id": "c020d5a9-b863-4224-96f0-475bef8972b8", "type": "concept", "title": "Approval criteria: feasibility, originality, ethical sourcing, and appropriate technical ambition"}], "description": "The capstone begins with a clear idea, audience, references, deliverables, and production plan."}, {"id": "f913503a-1caa-453a-80f0-cc2d7b382b9c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Production and refinement", "children": [{"id": "28455838-534e-40a8-b585-5bbe1cfafa6a", "type": "concept", "title": "Selections, masks, layers, color correction, retouching, compositing, type integration, and output settings"}, {"id": "aebd186b-d7cb-449d-94b5-299cd9933213", "type": "concept", "title": "Peer critique, instructor feedback, revision milestones, and technical troubleshooting"}, {"id": "dae7fb83-c8fa-4e6a-84e2-12087a69ebea", "type": "concept", "title": "Consistency across the series and alignment with the project concept"}], "description": "Students synthesize core Photoshop skills through a polished project that survives close inspection."}, {"id": "6a86072d-3d22-43e0-a3ab-c7e8757b3e97", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Final delivery and reflection", "children": [{"id": "12fa765e-353d-4658-a5fc-d630d01da2d5", "type": "concept", "title": "Layered PSD or PSB, print-ready PDF or TIFF, web exports, thumbnails, source log, permissions notes, and alt text"}, {"id": "040df4f2-d49b-4722-a5d7-1b8326113c04", "type": "concept", "title": "Artist or designer statement, process documentation, before/after evidence, and critique reflection"}, {"id": "646e56bd-afc5-4004-ad97-21ddabf3e071", "type": "concept", "title": "Portfolio case study, presentation sequence, and next-step improvement plan"}], "description": "The finished project should be delivered like professional work, with process and rationale visible."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$dimgjson$::jsonb,
